The popups are positioned with position: absolute relative to .shelf-scene. The CSS classes control where they appear — right now popup-books is left: 0, popup-music is left: 50% centered, popup-bag is right: 0.

The easiest fix is to add a style prop directly on each popup div to override the CSS position. That way you can nudge each one independently without touching the stylesheet.

Find each popup div and add a style like this:

jsx
{/* Books — appears near the left where the books are */}
<div className={`popup popup-books ${openPopup === "books" ? "open" : ""}`}
  style={{ top: "20px", left: "0px" }}>

{/* Bobo — appears in the center */}
<div className={`popup popup-music ${openPopup === "music" ? "open" : ""}`}
  style={{ top: "20px", left: "50%", transform: openPopup === "music" ? "translateX(-50%)" : "translateX(-50%) translateY(8px)" }}>

{/* Clock — appears center-right */}
<div className={`popup popup-clock ${openPopup === "clock" ? "open" : ""}`}
  style={{ top: "20px", right: "0px", left: "auto" }}>
The values that matter are top, left, and right. Play with these:

top → how far below the top of .shelf-scene the popup appears
left / right → horizontal position
